# A map's sorted view is what a read looks things up in, and it is held
# outside the arena for as long as the map lives. A thousand keys put in
# ascending order, none repeated, are already sorted, so the native build
# lets the pairs be the view: view_allocs reads 0 and held_peak_bytes 0,
# where a copy of the pairs was one view of 32,016 bytes. A decoded JSON
# object whose keys arrive in order is read the same way.
fn fill m 0
  m

fn fill m n
  fill (put m (1000 - n) n) (n - 1)

fn total _ 0 acc
  acc

fn total m n acc
  total m (n - 1) (acc + m[n - 1])

pub play = print "{total (fill {} 1000) 1000 0}"
